### Ranked Objections & Settling Evidence

| Rank | Objection | Core Mechanism | Settling Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | **Q-Filter Paralyzes Demonstrators** | The legacy $r_2$ penalty (-13.7% $r_1$ break-even) ensures $Q(s, a_{\text{CF-EE}}) \ll \max_a Q(s, a)$. The Nair Q-filter evaluates to FALSE, shutting off supervised losses and collapsing D4 to D0. | Forward evaluate 1,000 `CF-EE` transitions through the frozen Q-network. Measure pass rate. If $<5\%$, the design is broken. |
| **2** | **CF-GUARD is an Arithmetic Phantom** | TS 38.133 interruption (142 ms) loses 0.47% bits; channel gain buys +14.6%. The 72:1 ratio ensures `CF-GUARD` actions match `CF-EE` $>95\%$ of the time. | Roll out 50 episodes of `CF-EE` and interruption-based `CF-GUARD`. If action Jaccard overlap $>0.85$, `CF-GUARD` is redundant. |
| **3** | **Bellman Violation on Ratio Estimands** | Ratios of accumulated sums cannot be optimized via additive 1-step Bellman equations without outer-loop Dinkelbach decoupling. | Prove policy ranking flips under uniform energy scaling unless parameterized as Two-Critic $(Q_B, Q_E)$. |

